# SAME70Q20B USB-CDC boot/connect smoke test. Exercises the
# CONFIG_ATSAM_USB firmware variant (duet3-6hc / duet3-6xd printer
# configs are USB+CAN-only on real hardware, no serial-mode firmware
# variant exists) against the local USBHS Renode peripheral
# (test/emulator/repl/same70_usbhs.cs). The peripheral uses a
# "skip-enum cheat" - inject a SET_CONFIGURATION SETUP packet on EP0
# so klipper's CDC stack reaches bulk-active without a full USB host
# emulation - then exposes BULK_IN/BULK_OUT as a UART pipe to the
# host pty via UARTBase. The companion same70_smoke.test covers the
# CONFIG_ATSAM_SERIAL path; both share the same .repl (USBHS is
# resident unconditionally and stays idle when the firmware never
# touches it).
#
# This was the PR's long-standing known-blocked test; it now passes
# (3/3 on a clean host) after fixing a two-sided SysTick-vs-DWT tension:
#   * The upstream platforms/cpus/sam_e70.repl declares the NVIC SysTick
#     at 450MHz, but klipper drives SysTick with CLKSOURCE=processor (the
#     300MHz core clock / CONFIG_CLOCK_FREQ) and reads DWT->CYCCNT (also
#     300MHz). At 450MHz the SysTick fires ~1.5x early, so
#     timer_dispatch_many busy-waits a far deadline while OTHER timers fall
#     >1ms behind DWT -> static_string_id 56 "Rescheduled timer in the
#     past" shutdown. same70q20b.repl now pins systickFrequency to 300MHz.
#   * At 300MHz the reason-56 shutdown is gone, but enumeration used to
#     break: the USBHS model only injected its synthetic SET_CONFIGURATION
#     SETUP on a *spontaneous* DEVEPTISR[0] read, which the firmware only
#     did at the (wrong) 450MHz rate. same70_usbhs.cs now injects the SETUP
#     the moment the firmware arms RXSTPES on the allocated EP0
#     (handle_end_reset writes DEVEPTCFG[0]|ALLOC then DEVEPTIER[0]=RXSTPES
#     back to back), so enumeration self-starts independent of SysTick rate.
# Confirmed not the cause and not needed: MaximumBlockSize /
# SetGlobalQuantum / MIPS knobs. This test stays free-run; its
# deterministic-tick sibling same70_usb_tick.test drives the same USB-CDC
# host link under tick lockstep (the renode ARM tick byte-shuttle now
# survives identify over USB-CDC - see that test's header).
DICTIONARY same70q20b-usb.dict
CONFIG same70_usb_smoke.cfg
EMULATOR same70_usb_smoke.fixture.json

# A few harmless gcode lines so klippy gets past klippy:ready.
M114
M105
M105
M105

# klippy connected and stayed connected long enough to do the
# clocksync handshake against the firmware's generic/armcm_timer view
# transported over the synthetic USBHS bulk endpoints.
EXPECT_LOG_CONTAINS "Loaded MCU 'mcu'"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Internal error"
EXPECT_LOG_NOT_CONTAINS "Klippy is shutdown"
